.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt LIBXO 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xo_no_setlocale ,
.Nm xo_update_locale
.Nd control libxo's use of the locale
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxo
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libxo/xo.h
.Ft void
.Fn xo_no_setlocale "void"
.Ft void
.Fn xo_update_locale "int reset"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm libxo
automatically initializes the locale based on the setting of the
environment variables
.Ev LC_CTYPE ,
.Ev LANG ,
and
.Ev LC_ALL .
The first of this
list of variables is used and if none of the variables are set, the locale
defaults to
.Em UTF-8 .
The caller may wish to avoid this behavior, and
can do so by calling the
.Fn xo_no_setlocale
function.
This also clears any values
.Nm libxo
has cached from the locale, except those given with the
.Dq grouping
option.
.Pp
.Nm libxo
caches values it takes from the locale: the decimal point, the
thousands separator and grouping, and whether the codeset is UTF-8.
These are loaded when
.Nm libxo
first initializes, whether it set the locale itself or the caller did
(after calling
.Fn xo_no_setlocale ) .
A caller that changes the locale after that point, with
.Xr setlocale 3 ,
should call
.Fn xo_update_locale
with
.Fa reset
false to refresh them.
After that,
.Nm libxo
never calls
.Xr setlocale 3
itself, so calling it before
.Nm libxo
initializes also keeps
.Nm libxo
from setting the locale from the environment.
.Pp
With
.Fa reset
true,
.Fn xo_update_locale
undoes
.Fn xo_no_setlocale
(and any earlier
.Fn xo_update_locale ) :
.Nm libxo
sets the locale from the environment, as it does when it
initializes, and loads its values.
.Pp
A thousands separator and grouping given with the
.Dq grouping
option (see
.Xr xo_options 7 )
override the locale's and are not changed by
.Fn xo_update_locale ,
with either value of
.Fa reset .
The UTF-8 setting of the default handle is made when it is created,
and is not changed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr setlocale 3 ,
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr xo_open_container 3 ,
.Xr xo_open_list 3 ,
.Xr xo_format 5 ,
.Xr xo_options 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm libxo
library first appeared in
.Fx 11.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
